Cell["XMLMatchQ::badpat: The pattern should be an XMLPattern, an XMLElement pattern, an XMLDocument pattern, a list pattern for a list of elements, or a CSS selector string that describes one element, or alternatives of these, any of them named, with a condition pat /; test or a test pat?f. A rule gives a value, not a test. A CSS selector such as \"nav a\" or \"ul > li\" looks above the element, which a lone element does not have; use XMLCases or XMLPosition to search a tree with it. Child, Adjacent and Sibling were removed in version 4; a test of an element's children constrains them, as in XMLPattern[\"ul\", _, {___, XMLPattern[\"li\"], ___}], and XMLCases searches a tree with a rule, as in XMLPattern[\"ul\", _, {___, x : XMLPattern[\"li\"], ___}] :> x. Got x:XMLPattern[\"a\"] :> x.", "Message", "MSG"],

Cell[BoxData["$Failed"], "Output"]}, Open]],

